---
import Logo from '../components/Logo.astro'
import '../styles/global.css'
import ArrowLeft from '@lucide/astro/icons/arrow-left'
const REPO = 'https://github.com/kasvith/setflow'
const h2 = 'mt-8 mb-2 text-[1.15rem] font-bold'
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Setflow · privacy</title>
    <meta name="description" content="What Setflow stores and where. Everything stays in your browser." />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  </head>
  <body class="bg-ground text-ink">
    <main class="wrap max-w-[680px] py-12 pb-24">
      <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-muted hover:text-ink"><ArrowLeft size={16} /> <Logo size={18} /> Setflow</a>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-[2.4rem] font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-1 text-muted">Last updated 7 September 2026</p>

      <p class="mt-5 text-[1.15rem]">
        Setflow does not collect, store or transmit any of your data. There is no server behind it. The only
        place anything is kept is the extension's own storage in your browser, and you can wipe it by
        uninstalling.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>What stays on your device</h2>
      <p class="mb-2.5">
        Setflow keeps the plans you make: phase names, durations and colours, start, sunrise and sunset times,
        journey names, and the URL and title of the YouTube Music playlists you plan on. Presets and unsaved
        drafts are kept the same way.
      </p>
      <p>
        All of it lives in Chrome's extension storage on your device. Nothing is sent to a server. Setflow has
        no backend, no account, no analytics and no third-party code that runs at all.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>What it reads</h2>
      <p>
        On <code class="rounded-md bg-sheet-2 px-1.5 py-px font-mono text-[0.9em]">music.youtube.com</code> the extension reads the playlist page you have open to find the track
        list and each track's length, so it can mark the tracks. It does not read anything on other sites and
        does not read your YouTube account.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Permissions</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 marker:text-muted">
        <li><b>storage</b> to save your plans on your device.</li>
        <li><b>activeTab</b> and <b>scripting</b> to mark up the playlist page you are on when you open the popup.</li>
        <li><b>music.youtube.com</b> so the marking works on YouTube Music and nowhere else.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class={h2}>Export</h2>
      <p>
        Export JSON writes a file to your computer with the tracks and times of the current plan. It is created
        locally and goes nowhere unless you share it.
      </p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Removing your data</h2>
      <p>Uninstalling the extension deletes everything it stored. Delete individual journeys and presets in the Library.</p>

      <h2 class={h2}>Questions</h2>
      <p>Setflow is open source. Read the code or ask on <a class="underline decoration-muted underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-ink" href={`${REPO}/issues`} rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.</p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
